// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Tundra 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1662180905" "One of Paragon City's heroes thinks he can catch you unaware by ambushing you on your first task from Arachnos. He'd better think again!"
// GroupDescription :
"P12711891" "Longbow"
// DisplayNames :
"P2759077259" "Tundra"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Snow_Maiden 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1398927120" "A nature spirit joined with a young woman, Snow Maiden uses the icy power of winter to fight crime."
// GroupDescription :
"P4059873720" "Hero"
// DisplayNames :
"P65249005" "Snow Maiden"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Strongheart 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3208149882" "This young hero's incredible might and impenetrable skin make him a formidable foe."
// DisplayNames :
"P3394325198" "Strongheart"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Experiment_236 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3311782538" "Experiment 236 is a creation of Dr. Dmitri Krylov, a Russian scientist who came to the Rogue Isles to make money by creating super-powered villains. Experiment 236 did not survive the transformation process with his sanity intact, and has since gone on a fiery rampage!"
// GroupDescription :
"P968514626" "Krylov's Creations"
// DisplayNames :
"P3810723330" "Experiment 236"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_ElectroShock 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1885595059" "Electroshock is a hero created by the super-science of Dr. Dmitri Krylov. Electroshock was originally a villain who came to Krylov seeking super-powers, but in the end decided to become a hero in Paragon City."
// DisplayNames :
"P665777564" "ElectroShock"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Ranger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P662179107" "The Ranger thinks she can stop you from rescuing Olivia Darque. She's wrong."
// DisplayNames :
"P915202013" "The Ranger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Ace_McKnight_Villain 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3985281012" "Ace McKnight is the source of Willy Wheeler's missions, and has gotten himself in trouble! You need to get him out of this mess!"
// GroupDescription :
"P297633287" "Rogue Isles Informer"
// DisplayNames :
"P381354815" "Ace McKnight"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Ace_McKnight_Hero 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3843140026" "Ace McKnight is the source of Willy Wheeler's missions. Unfortunately, McKnight has turned out to be an undercover Longbow agent and needs to be taken down!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Ace_McKnight_Hero_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1269208191" "Ace McKnight is an elite agent for the Freedom Corp organization known as Longbow. He is a master of infiltration and escape techniques."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Dragons_Tail 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P503143189" "The Dragon's Tail is desperately seeking the antidote to a plague in Paragon City. Of course, you're being paid to pick up the same antidote. So someone's gotta lose."
// DisplayNames :
"P3972818654" "The Dragon's Tail"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Blue_Phazer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1289298935" "Blue Phazer is a hero working with Longbow in the Rogue Isles. She is known to possess a robotic super-suit which allows her to manipulate high-energy fields."
// DisplayNames :
"P441131660" "Blue Phazer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Blue_Phazer_NoXP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayClassName :
"P2664220932" "Boss"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Golden_Sphinx 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3578818490" "Golden Sphinx is a hero working with Longbow in the Rogue Isles. He is known to possess an ancient Egyptian amulet which grants him supernatural powers."
// DisplayNames :
"P1683671025" "Golden Sphinx"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Golden_Sphinx_NoXP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_LeoKnight 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1134299110" "This massive Tanker is the older brother of Longbow Agent Caspian. The same Caspian you captured for Vargas. He's angry, he's tough, and beating the villain who caught his little brother is his top priority."
// DisplayNames :
"P2302506059" "LeoKnight"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Spinnerette 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2266660919" "Spinnerette is a lieutenant of the Scrapyarder hero known as Iron Widow. She is a champion of the Scrapyarder cause in Sharkhead."
// GroupDescription :
"P4226107325" "Scrapyarders"
// DisplayNames :
"P1612381761" "Spinnerette"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Iron_Widow 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P250320881" "Iron Widow is the secretive leader of the Scrapyarders ever since the murder of Scrapyard at the hands of the deadly Captain Mako. She handles most of the Scrapyarder operations out of Paragon City to avoid death at the hands of Cage Consortium and Arachnos assassins who find her agenda to disruptive to operations on the Rogue Isles."
// DisplayNames :
"P626619535" "Iron Widow"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Iron_Widow_Villain 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Agent_Caspian_Low 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1811119001" "Agent Caspian is an elite agent for the Freedom Corp organization known as Longbow. He is a master of infiltration and escape techniques."
// DisplayNames :
"P2078087827" "Agent Caspian"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Agent_X 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2573547483" "Agent X is a renowned Longbow super-spy. His technical skills are phenomenal, with a gadget or gizmo available for any occasion."
// DisplayNames :
"P1124522932" "Agent X"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Agent_X_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Agent_X_NoXP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Ether 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2864211849" "If you can take out this fledgeling heroine, you'll prove yourself to Operative Rutger."
// DisplayNames :
"P1378419333" "Ether"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Sidewinder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2042439627" "Sidewinder is one of Operative Rutger's assets. She's been undercover in Longbow for some time, but her cover's been blown. You'll have to extract her."
// GroupDescription :
"P1902797650" "Arachnos"
// DisplayNames :
"P2095442874" "Sidewinder"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_White_Lightning 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3532059402" "White Lightning was a fool to think he could defect to Longbow without bringing down the wrath of Arachnos. Take him out, and you'll be moving up in the world."
// DisplayNames :
"P1485445850" "White Lightning"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Theadora_Marcone 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1831788424" "A Family cousin, the love of Johnny's life, and a closet superheroine: Theadora Marcone leads a busy life. A shame you'll have to take her out."
// DisplayNames :
"P3339538231" "Theadora Marcone"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Dr_Advance 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P828964136" "Dr. Advance uses his suit of space/time manipulating powered armor to help Longbow explore dangerous extremes of science!"
// DisplayNames :
"P4190062674" "Dr. Advance"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Shockstorm 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2034252951" "Shockstorm is a hero working with Longbow in the Rogues Isles. He coordinates operations out of the Longbow base of Agincourt on the Nerva Archipelago."
// DisplayNames :
"P2954512943" "Shockstorm"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Biopulse 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P852750701" "Biopulse is one of the rare Infected who drank from the toxic cesspools on Mercy Island and actually manifested super powers! He now hopes to champion the cause of the Infected on Mercy Island as a hero."
// GroupDescription :
"P792233903" "Infected"
// DisplayNames :
"P874681223" "Biopulse"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Doctor_Geist 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1790348915" "Doctor Geist is a mad scientist working for Arachnos on a project involving mutant spiders! He is also a long time rival of his former colleague, Doctor Creed."
// DisplayNames :
"P2613354304" "Doctor Geist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Pizzazz 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P735635085" "Pizzazz is a Magic Origin hero who has come under Mage Killer's Zuhkara's purview. Destroy her!"
// DisplayNames :
"P179796100" "Pizzazz"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Civic_Max_Action 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3164744526" "The leader of the amazing superteam called the Civic Squad, Max Action is a one-man war on crime. Though he's lead the Civic Squad for several years, Max Action's true history is a closely guarded secret. Rumors claim he may be a genetically engineered super-soldier, a movie action hero who escaped to the real world, or just a determined man who's pushed human ability to it's limit. One thing's beyond debate, though: his advanced martial arts abilities and finely honed reflexes place him among the most dangerous one-on-one combatants in the world."
// GroupDescription :
"P805541063" "Civic Squad"
// DisplayNames :
"P2189224511" "Max Action"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Civic_Electrixie 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1285219951" "Trixie Watts had gone sailing around the world to try and forget all those she'd lost in the Rikti war. But when she was caught in a radioactive thunderstorm following an illegal Nemesis Army underwater atomic test, she found her life transformed. Trixie had gained the power to control electricity itself, and more importantly, the courage to make a difference."
// DisplayNames :
"P2240878245" "Electrixie"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Civic_Mechannie 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3064900858" "The robotic 'daughter' of crimefighting inventor and gunslinger Sergio 'Sixtygun' Seiger, Mechannie Seiger carries on her father's crusade to bring justice to any outlaw who crosses her path. Her robotic body makes her nearly indestructible, but it's her fun-loving attitude and a heart the size of Texas that makes her truly unstoppable. When she's not fighting crime, Mechannie can often be seen at DJ Zero's Paragon Dance Party, dancing the night away."
// DisplayNames :
"P3139696816" "Mechannie"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Civic_Gravidian 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P596367282" "Discovering you're the son of an alien is a difficult thing in the years following the Rikti war. For young Tensor Fields, it was the first thing in his life that made sense. He trained his native gravity-altering abilities under his father's tutelage, and took up the traditional heroic garb of his homeworld as his own. Now he upholds the high ideals of an advanced civilization as Gravidian!"
// DisplayNames :
"P4089042558" "Gravidian"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Civic_Energeist 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1643602021" "Born on a battlefield of the Rikti War, the strange being known only as Energeist is the living energy of dozens of meta human powers given physical form and sentient will. For a full year he travelled the ruins left behind by the war, absorbing spent power, gaining strength, and battling those who would take advantage of the the desperate people displaced by the war. After meeting the Civic Squad, he joined their team to find a place for himself in the world."
// DisplayNames :
"P463465524" "Energeist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Civic_Decibelle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4294611879" "Marybell Eddison had been singing since she was little, and loved to make people happy with her song. Then her mutation kicked in, and her beautiful voice became a weapon capable of demolishing buildings. Some might have lapsed into despair, but the kindly words of her family pastor helped Marybell see her power for the gift it was. While she may not be able to make people happy with her song, now she can protect them with the power of her voice as Decibelle!"
// DisplayNames :
"P848183476" "Decibelle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Civic_Rosewood 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2001494972" "The strange plant-woman called Rosewood was found as a seedling in an abandoned greenhouse in the back woods of Oregon by a high school science club on a backpacking trip. She was raised by that class and succeeding classes, and eventually graduated from that very school with top honors and a scholarship to Paragon City University. She soon found herself hunted by the Circle of Thorns, and decided to take the fight back to them, and anyone who would endanger the helpess."
// DisplayNames :
"P3462551197" "Rosewood"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Civic_Dr_Psychotron 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2265986739" "Buster Melville was a promising medical student with a great future ahead of him. That is, until he was kidnapped by the Clockwork king and became the subject of the mad machine master's experiments to create loyal human subjects. Things looked hopeless until a battle with the mental heroine Aurora Borealis caused a feed-back loop that not only destroyed his control circuits, but opened the psionic potential latent in his mind. After finishing medical school, Buster decided to take up the heroic mantle himself, and now fights any would-be tyrannt as Dr. Psychotron!"
// DisplayNames :
"P1499674401" "Dr. Psychotron"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_The_Quest 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2945556604" "Young orphan Jimmy Blankenship grew up in the Rogue Isles, surving by his street smarts and the kind help of Westin Phipps' Haven House. He might have even found a life in the isles, until the day Arachnos troops took the woman he loved away for forcible induction into Fortunatas. He nearly died trying to save her, but still failed. On the run from Arachons, he escaped the Isles and found his way to Paragon City. There he trained under combat masters and found his personal desire for revenge transformed into a larger quest for justice."
// DisplayNames :
"P1349515680" "The Quest"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Brickhouse 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1822308212" "Brickhouse grew up in East Germany, but when the wall fell moved to the United States. He recently was hired by Freedom Corps to help with some overseas operations due to his dual citizenship."
// GroupDescription :
// DisplayNames :
"P2562134267" "Brikhaus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Mindspider 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3265938226" "Mindspider was a government agent working for the DATA division of the FBSA. After a few too many 'disciplinary actions' she retired from the FBSA and went freelance. She can be found working for various hero groups, including Longbow, if the price is right."
// DisplayNames :
"P428065473" "Mindspider"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Salvo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4081395771" "Salvo is another magic-based hero who has caught the attention of Mage-Killer Zuhkara. Destroy him!"
// DisplayNames :
"P3752739485" "Salvo"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Fusionette_Pet 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2455260869" "Fusionette is one of the Nuclear 90; 90 children from around the world all born in one year with an unusual mutation that gives them natural magnetic nuclear fusion reactors for hearts, and the ability to channel energy from their internal reactor for a variety of super powers. Like many of the Nuclear 90, Fusionette has decided to use her powers for the betterment of mankind as a hero. She's focused on her energy blasts and has recently developed the power of flight."
// GroupDescription :
"P1530484312" "Paragon Heroine"
// DisplayNames :
"P12622965" "Fusionette"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Fusionette 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Doc_Delilah 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3551457857" "Doctor Delilah Stein was born with her Herculean strength and incredible physical resistance. She fought evil as a heroine for a time, but eventually found her real calling: History and Archeology. Now she combines her past life and her education into a new career as an historian of meta-human history, and an archeologist of the unusual. Dr. Stein recently began investigating the hero bases lost in the destruction of Overbrook, looking for clues to fill in the history of pre-Rikti War heroes and villains."
// GroupDescription :
"P3914140580" "Dept. of Archeology"
// DisplayNames :
"P1035024325" "Doc Delilah"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Lk_Onik 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2592277646" "Lk'Onik is a mystery even to his fellow Rikti. Though a life-long member of the Rikti Lineage of War, he left the military during the Restructurist/Traditionalist split for reasons of his own. He has been with the Traditionalists ever since, working towards peace."
// GroupDescription :
"P2995219246" "Rikti Traditionalist"
// DisplayNames :
"P711310533" "Psi-Scout Lk'Onik"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Miss_Liberty_EliteBoss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1536406415" "Daughter to the well known Statesman, Miss Liberty grew up around some of the greatest heroes mankind has ever seen. It is no surprise that she grew up to be one herself. Inheriting the sacred girdle from her mother and the superhuman abilities of the gods from her father, Miss Liberty is a force for justice and equality across America."
// DisplayNames :
"P2768490694" "Miss Liberty"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Mender_Lazarus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P986316996" "Mender Lazarus is a time traveler who lost his sense of continuity some time ago. He is still a brilliant scientist and historian, he just occasionally puts the "effect" before the "cause.""
// GroupDescription :
"P2104234921" "Ouroboros"
// DisplayNames :
"P3110941004" "Mender Lazarus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Cyrus_Thompson 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2623336063" "Cyrus Thompson is a retired superhero who once went by the name Breakneck. His wife gave him this name, not because of his super speed, but because "If you don't give up this nonsense, you're going to break your fool neck.""
// DisplayNames :
"P2371566604" "Cyrus Thompson"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Kadabra_Kill 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P165401570" "In all his travels around the world and to realms unknown, Kadabra Kill seeks a single prize, the salvation of his wife, Sigil. Long ago, when they were both young and foolish, she gave up her soul to save his own. Soon she must pay the ultimate price."
// DisplayNames :
"P1432690416" "Kadabra Kill"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Sigil 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1333890919" "Sigil's soul is marked by a demon from the dark void. She signed a pact, her soul for her lover's life. Ever since, her and her husband, Kadabra Kill, have spent their adult lives seeking a loop hole in the bargain. So far, they have come up empty handed."
// DisplayNames :
"P2639129193" "Sigil"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_LeoKnight_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_LeoKnight_Boss_NoXP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Alysonde 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2125922498" "Once a young explorer, Marissa Sorensen was well-known amongst the scientific community for discoveries relating the the relationship between the gods of the various pantheons and a strange location from which they drew their power. One day, Marissa herself discovered this location and became the Huntress, Alysonde. She is renowned among the heroes of the world for her selflessness, but her history as an explorer has left her with many enemies."
// GroupDescription :
"P240425177" "The Protectors"
// DisplayNames :
"P1125762966" "Alysonde"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Alysonde_Weak 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Apex 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1291615942" "Apex has been a covert member of Vanguard for quite some time now. He has proven himself multiple times to be trustworthy and capable of leading initiatives that are given to him. Lady Grey and Dark Watcher have come to rely on him to lead squads on the most important of missions."
// GroupDescription :
"P2154096770" "Vanguard"
// DisplayNames :
"P273280760" "Apex"

