"P2927463380" "Scrapper Hero"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Sister_Psyche_Tutorial 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P105907675" "Even in her childhood, it was obvious that Sister Psyche was blessed. The tremendous scope of her mental powers was far beyond that of any hero, past or present. When the Rikti War descended, Sister Psyche knew she had to make her gift count. She did, but at a price. She exhausted her powers so thoroughly that she fell into a coma. A young heroine named Aurora Borealis offered to play host to Sister Psyche's projected mental self. Of course, this situation could not last forever. Now back in her own body, Sister Psyche has dedicated herself to helping to shape the tremendous gifts of the young Aurora. It's a responsibility she takes seriously, as well as a consolation for the loss of her former protoge, Malaise. When the psychic link between the two women was first disrupted, Sister Psyche lost her mental control over Malaise's dual personalities. The evil Malaise reasserted himself, and quickly made his departure. His present whereabouts are as yet unknown."
// GroupDescription :
"P4246764481" "Freedom Phalanx"
// DisplayNames :
"P3744943569" "Sister Psyche"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Back_Alley_Brawler_Tutorial 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1556005063" "One of the most veteran heroes in Paragon City, the Brawler is in semi-retirement, training the next generation of heroes. Though he rarely goes into the field these days, his power and fighting skills are still as potent as ever."
// GroupDescription :
"P1412809039" "Independent"
// DisplayNames :
"P3365661715" "Back Alley Brawler"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Tielekku 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1840961032" "Ancient myths say that the goddess Tielekku was the first being to harness the power of magic. She then taught her magic to other gods and mortals and used her abilities to defeat an evil pantheon of gods, banishing them to the spirit world.<br><br>Tielekku is a powerful entity, though it is rumored that her power has faded over the centuries due to the distribution of magic."
// DisplayClassName :
"P3197541287" "Goddess"
// GroupDescription :
"P928546890" "Ancient"
// DisplayNames :
"P1082604521" "Tielekku"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Devoured_Super_Pyriss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3664158211" "Pyriss was once an impressionable young would-be heroine, until Peter Themari and a truly depraved villain tricked her into turning against her allies and becoming a villain herself. It seems that her villainous life left her at the mercy of the devouring Earth, who consumed her and transformed her into what she is now. The scientist Vernon von Grun has experimented on Pyriss, trying to discover the secret behind the Devouring Earth. As a result, von Grun has triggered parts of Pyriss's old personality to resurface, while also empowering her beyond her normal proportions."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2393090127" "Devoured"
// DisplayNames :
"P4134727936" "Super Devoured Pyriss"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_BlueSteel 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2286739925" "Blue Steel was originally a promising beat cop with the Paragon Police Department before he grew into the role of hero. He was affiliated with Back Alley Brawler and the Regulators, and led initiatives to curb gang activity in Paragon City. He led one of the early crackdowns against the Clockwork, though has rarely spoken of the encounter. The PPD works very closely with Blue Steel, though he finds time between assisting the force and training newer heroes to lend a hand in otherwise impossible situations."
// GroupDescription :
"P1492594559" "PPD"
// DisplayNames :
"P1887178065" "Blue Steel"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Lord_Recluse_NoScale 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2936484795" "The Master of Evil, the Count of Cruel, the Archvillain of Anarchy. Lord Recluse has been called many things. But the people of the Rogue Isles know him as their lord and ruler. Lord Recluse has a mysterious tie with Paragon City's own Statesman - some even claim they were once close companions. Their hatred for one another certainly belies a secret perhaps best left buried."
// DisplayClassName :
"P843870427" "Archvillain"
// DisplayNames :
"P2939457459" "Lord Recluse"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Honoree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3925749949" "The Honoree was formerly Hero 1, the hero who was sent to the Rikti homeworld and successfully destroyed the bridge between their world and ours. Hero 1 was captured on the Ritki homeworld and subjected to mutations similar to what the Lost undergo, creating this new abomination. He is now back in Vanguard care, and with the help of several powerful psychics, is being used by Vanguard against high-level threats."
// DisplayNames :
"P608879005" "Honoree"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Mender_Silos_PraetorianClass 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P407378683" "Ouroboros' ability to time travel is entirely the work of the brilliant futurist, Mender Silos. He was the one who founded the group, brought its members back in time and is attempting to save everything. He is a stoic leader who seems to have the ability to look right through people as if they weren't there. The other members of Ouroboros say that this is because when Mender Silos looks a you he sees every 'when' you ever were and will be. Silos speaks little of his own time, only to say it is a cold, dark place where all that is living is too quickly burning out."
// DisplayNames :
"P2371005619" "Mender Silos"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Infinity 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1833484981" "Infinity commands the robots, all creations of his own hands. He seems to have a vendetta against the valley, one that you are caught in the middle of."
// GroupDescription :
"P3920075834" "The Robots"
// DisplayNames :
"P1015270809" "Infinity"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Infinity_NoTeleport 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Infinity_Cutscene 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Epoch 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P994122575" "This wise old man has taught you more about life and responsibility than anyone else. He is a kind soul until you push him, then his gifted powers come to the surface."
// GroupDescription :
"P2572987594" "Companion"
// DisplayNames :
"P1933368747" "Epoch"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Mercenary 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3627529228" "A man with a mysterious past, Mercenary has just as much reason to confront Infinity and his army of robots as you do."
// DisplayNames :
"P1403447585" "Mercenary"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericHeroes_Whispering_Coyote 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2982119577" "Whispering Coyote is a spirit animal who is very knowledgeable about the spirit world."
// DisplayClassName :
"P945658005" "Spirit Companion"
