// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Malta_Slinger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4073927390" "Slinger is one of Malta's engineering geniuses, with excellent knowledge of advanced robotics and weapons. Some suspect he had a direct hand in the development of the infamous Titan robots."
// GroupDescription :
"P3589285115" "Malta"
// DisplayNames :
"P1420108846" "Slinger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Archon_Burkholder 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3200127666" "Archon Burkholder is a relic from another villainous group that was recently subsumed by the Council. Nevertheless, he seems to have made a place for himself in the new regime. His obsession with robotics led him to carve off his own arm and replace it with one of steel; it also led him to create this terrifying robot factory. To prevent the launch of the giant Zenith Mech Man, you must defeat Burkholder."
// GroupDescription :
"P1095527038" "Council"
// DisplayNames :
"P3920060084" "Archon Burkholder"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Nosferatu 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3019526964" "Few truly appreciate the genius of Nosferatu's super soldier program, and none more so than himself. Nosferatu was so entranced by his ability to create the super strong Vampyri that he became one of them. He has since improved upon his original design by granting himself several new abilities. He can mesmerize his opponents, leaving them helpless. Some say he can even siphon off the life force of his foes."
// DisplayNames :
"P1215451297" "Nosferatu"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Bladestorm 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3176408357" "Bladestorm is a psychic blade-wielding hitman for the syndicate."
// GroupDescription :
"P3557448881" "Syndicate"
// DisplayNames :
"P1370962095" "Tub Ci"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_P_Siege 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3281617799" "The masterpiece of Neuron, Siege is the most advanced android ever created on Praetorian Earth. Neuron used Tyrant's DNA patterns to create him, making him virtually indestructible and extremely loyal."
// GroupDescription :
"P1833469820" "Praetorians"
// DisplayNames :
"P2798099443" "Siege"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_P_Nightstar 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P510360342" "This android is the creation of Anti-Matter as a testament to his love for Dominatrix. Nightstar is patterned after her in the same way that Siege is patterned after Tyrant. Neuron considers it an inferior design but Anti-Matter knows that one day victory will be his."
// DisplayNames :
"P1904626672" "Nightstar"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Desideratus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2929432719" "Desideratus was once a well-regarded historian and classicist, but he never felt that he had garnered the recognition he truly deserved. Indeed, his intellect was matched only by his jealousy, leading him to covet all the things he felt should have been his. When the link to the power of the gods was uncovered, he was enraged when that power chose Rhiannon over him and this rage informed his every action since. He has spent years accumulating money and power, learning ancient secrets and developing new technologies, all in an effort to make the world pay for something over a perceived slight over which no one had any control."
// GroupDescription :
"P1064382461" "The Dominion"
// DisplayNames :
"P3550931034" "Desideratus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Trapdoor 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2038831509" "Since Trapdoor's escape from Arachnos, he has made an alliance with the Council to find ways to improve his nacent Incarnate abilities. One new trick he's picked up is the ability to teleport himself to multiple places at once, bifurcating his body to recuperate from enemy attacks."
// GroupDescription :
"P3487295804" "Incarnate Wannabe"
// DisplayNames :
"P1583502422" "Trapdoor"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Trapdoor_Bifurcation 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2712298794" "Trapdoor has used the power of teleportation and correspondence to appear to be in multiple places at once. While he is not fully concentrating in those areas, he is able to use the respite to regenerate himeself."
// GroupDescription :
"P3110684666" "Bifurcation"
// DisplayNames :
"P3316249698" "Trapdoor Bifurcation"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Leonard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P754163475" "Leonard was once the bodyguard for a man named Thomas Mane. After Thomas Mane's death, Leonard has decided to stay in the Isles and offer his services to those individuals who have his trust."
// DisplayClassName :
"P625106198" "Bodyguard"
// GroupDescription :
"P856622151" "Freelancers"
// DisplayNames :
"P2561024276" "Leonard"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Porter_Flame_Jumpbot 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2495677914" "The Jump Bots are a recent addition to the mercenary Sky Raiders' arsenal. Their effectiveness in combat has allowed the Raiders to greatly expand operations. Well armed and armored, the Jump Bots earned their name from their leaping ability, which allows them tremendous maneuverability."
// DisplayNames :
"P3524264305" "Jump Bot Incinerator"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - GenericVillains_Porter_Gun_Jumpbot 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2282206667" "Assault Jump Bot"

