// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Belladonna 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4151204414" "One of the deadliest covert agents in the world, Belladonna has proven herself a most capable spy and killer for the Resistance. Though her past is a well kept secret, Belladonna makes it clear that she has no love for Tyrant or his lackeys. Rumors abound that she was trained by Chimera; Tyrant's Praetor of Intelligence and widely considered the deadliest assassin in the world. Belladonna will one day put that title to the test."
// DisplayClassName :
"P1165603828" "Assassin"
// DisplayNames :
"P2250471757" "Belladonna Vetrano"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Warworks_ACU_A 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P388952242" "The most advanced of the Warworks shock troopers. These towering androids carry a heavy PGMP Rifle that is capable of delivering a deadly neurotoxin payload."
// GroupDescription :
"P2699826295" "WarWorks"
// DisplayNames :
"P1313638232" "ACU"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Mender_Silos 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3835112650" "Ouroboros' ability to time travel is entirely the work of the brilliant futurist, Mender Silos.  He was the one who founded the group, brought its members back in time and is attempting to save everything. He is a stoic leader who seems to have the ability to look right through people as if they weren't there. The other members of Ouroboros say that this is because when Mender Silos looks at you he sees every 'when' you ever were and will be.<br><br>Silos speaks little of his own time, only to say it is a cold, dark place where all that is living is too quickly burning out."
// DisplayClassName :
"P1634741266" "Mender"
// GroupDescription :
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Mender_Ramiel 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P824250120" "Mender Ramiel comes from a far future version of Ouroboros. In that future, he has seen the efforts of Mender Silos here in this time period have some real effect, bringing forth the attention of the power behind the Incarnates, the Well of the Furies. He has come from the far future to herald this event, and to possibly increase its impact in the future."
// DisplayNames :
"P2674279424" "Mender Ramiel"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Praetorian_Prisoner_Male 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1898654383" "This pitiful soul has been imprisoned for Cole-knows how long in the Behavioral Adjustment Facility."
// GroupDescription :
"P2480328718" "Behavioral Adjustees"
// DisplayNames :
"P1576511405" "Prisoner"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Praetorian_Prisoner_Female 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Robert_Flores 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P748568847" "Robert Flores is a small-time journalist in Nova Praetoria. He's always been in the shadow of his older sister, Jessica Flores, but that doesn't stop him from trying to pick up leads to investigate. What <i>does</i> stop him is the hand of Emperor Cole coming down on his investigations when they get too 'in-depth'."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2242902095" "Journalist"
// GroupDescription :
"P1196525362" "Resistance"
// DisplayNames :
"P1519717787" "Robert Flores"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Tunnel_Rat 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1685846679" "Tunnel Rat has been given the task of helping get people out of Praetoria City. She spent most of her life living in the tunnels, giving her heightened vision in the dark and an incredible sense of smell.<br><br>Unfortunately, she must permanently wear a re-breather, due to all of the toxic fumes she has inhaled over the years.<br><br>Her time in the tunnels has made her an invaluable asset to the Resistance. Though she is one of the more... paranoid members, having seen many of her friends torn apart by ghouls."
// DisplayClassName :
"P1705657162" "Smuggler"
// DisplayNames :
"P399962985" "Tunnel Rat"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Jessica_Flores 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1780848688" "Jessica Flores is an independent investigative reporter whose agenda is uncovering the media's lies about the Resistance movement and showing people the truth of things. This is a dangerous job, however, and she has adopted several pen names under which she writes her articles in order to hide her identity. She hopes to one day crack the wall of censorship that TPN imposses over any and all stories involving the Resistance movement and its believers."
// DisplayNames :
"P2657666630" "Jessica Flores"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Chance_McKnight 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1483868737" "Chance McKnight is one of the most dedicated officers in the Ministry of Intelligence. He's taken on the responsibility of going undercover into the Syndicate, doing questionable acts that go against everything he believes in in order to get a chance to accomplishing something greater; the arrest of the Syndicate's shadowy leaders. For the past six months McKnight has worked his way up the ladder of leadership and is very close to accomplishing his goal."
// DisplayClassName :
"P3880432537" "Agent"
// GroupDescription :
"P2422482652" "Praetorian Police"
// DisplayNames :
"P1736376830" "Chance McKnight"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Mr_G 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P355062142" "Mr. G is known to be an enigmatic man within the government of Praetoria. He also seems to know just what exactly is going on. Some say he has his pulse on everything that happens in Imperial City. Regardless of rumors, all of the people of Imperial trust Mr. G with their safety - and their lives."
// GroupDescription :
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Emperor_Cole 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1548374938" "Marcus Cole came from the streets of Shroud City with nothing to his name, and ascended to the ultimate throne of power. He pulled the planet back from nuclear annihilation, ended the Hamidon Wars with his own indomitable will, and created a perfect utopian society for all those who follow him. Cole has had many titles in his long life, Soldier, Hero, President, Consul, and for the last 25 years, Emperor of Earth."
// DisplayClassName :
"P3238307228" "Emperor"
// DisplayNames :
"P1125736841" "Emperor Marcus Cole"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Splice 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P612743642" "A reclusive technophile, Splice's skill with a soldering iron has saved more lives than almost anyone else in the Resistance. She invented 'blueboxes', cheap home-made devices that allow the Resistance to send and receive messages over Praetoria City's power lines, known lovingly as 'The Static'. She's also pioneered a technique to allow cellular phones to function off the grid, a feat she boasts to have figured out in only five minutes flat.<br><br>Currently she's working on reprogramming captured clockwork androids. Of course, since the things pack dangerous weaponry the specimens her allies bring in for her are usually less than functional."
// DisplayClassName :
"P1024164993" "Hacker"
// DisplayNames :
"P2280926866" "Splice"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Swift_Cut 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4257061508" "Swift Cut is the woman who has hired you to help her get out of the Whispering Hand. Keeping her alive will lead to a fairly large pay day."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2061748292" "Ex-Assassin"
// GroupDescription :
"P3603767957" "Whispering Hand"
// DisplayNames :
"P274527963" "Swift Cut"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Arbiter_Daos 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1845152511" "Arbiter Daos is perhaps the most humorless man to ever walk the Rogue Isles. A devout servant of Arachnos, Daos is not loathe to take advantage of the impunity his position provides him. He often investigates groups and activities that, strictly speaking, lie outside his purview, but he does so in the knowledge that, whatever his reasons, Arachnos will stand beside him."
// DisplayClassName :
"P1767890595" "Arbiter"
// DisplayNames :
"P1396339461" "Arbiter Daos"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Fiona_Kal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2338874338" "Fiona Kal"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Jean_Louard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1281634695" "The agenda of this mysterious man is anyone's guess."
// DisplayNames :
"P145769542" "Jean Louard"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Alexis_Cole_Duncan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P694155135" "Alexis Cole-Duncan was once called Miss Liberty. She is the daughter of Statesman and the mother of Ms. Liberty. Alexis spent some time in retirement before picking back up the mantle of heroism, only this time it would be as a diplomat/negotiator. She works together with General Howard Aarons to calm various super-powered threats down, though unfortunately, most threats elevate to a hostile level before she even arrives at the scene."
// DisplayNames :
"P1652534247" "Alexis Cole-Duncan"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Jean_Louard_Combat 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1476408666" "Jean-Pierre 'Malaise' Lourdin was not always a hero. He began his career as a villain in Europe, using the twisted images in his mind to commit robberies. With INTERPOL hot on his trail he landed in Paragon City, where his broken thoughts were detected by Sister Psyche. She confronted him and after an intense battle was able to subdue him.  For years, he worked as a hero with the Vindicators, though many believed it was only a matter of time until his madness returned. They were, unfortunately, correct. Now, as his 'old' self, Malaise seeks to use his powers to terrorize those around him, all in the name of 'art', or so he claims."
// DisplayClassName :
"P1135554290" "Ex-Vindicator"
// GroupDescription :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Robert_Alderman 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1495786282" "Robert Alderman is a member of the city council, known for his firm stance on several unpopular issues. Many wonder if it's even possible for him to be re-elected in the next election."
// DisplayClassName :
"P1070118229" "Council Member"
// DisplayNames :
"P310715051" "Robert Alderman"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Detective_Hopp 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2971750802" "Detective Hopp is an investigator for the PPD. He recently was reported missing after looking into a suicide case that happened in Peregrine Island."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2216035317" "Detective"
// GroupDescription :
// DisplayNames :
"P2966937170" "Detective Hopp"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Max_Civilian 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3175654417" "This mysterious man seems to be a prime target for both the Knives of Vengeance and the Banished Pantheon"
// DisplayNames :
"P2772132969" "Max"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Lastri_Kayumanis 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P16080194" "While Lastri Kayumanis remains a new player in the Rogue Isles, her organization appears to have significant financial resources at its disposal. Less than a week after arriving in Sharkhead, she managed to establish a stable, wide-ranging smuggling operation, complete with a trained and loyal workforce. She has used this network to smuggle military-grade weaponry into the Rogue Isles under the nose of Arachnos, but it is unclear what purpose her employer has in mind for them."
// GroupDescription :
"P3027665111" "The Cottus Consortium"
// DisplayNames :
"P1628423499" "Lastri Kayumanis"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Warehouse_Worker 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3965660297" "From their dress, these men would appear to be simple warehouse workers, spending their time carrying and organizing crates of merchandise. Their clothes are plain, and they are unarmed. And yet, they show no signs of fear in the presence of heavily-armed Arachnos soldiers, and infamous Villains of the Rogue Isles... which is hardly expected behavior, for a simple warehouse worker."
// DisplayNames :
"P1884667546" "Warehouse Worker"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_NightWard_DeadChild 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// GroupDescription :
"P4189890620" "The Dead"
// DisplayNames :
"P2220064634" "Orphaned Spirit"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_James_Harvan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2721853349" "James Harvan is known as the leading expert in research on artifacts from the Archaic period of Ancient Greece. While his peers acknowledge that much of his work is groundbreaking, he is still seen as a fairly unorthodox figure in the field of archaeology. This is primarily due to his insistence that much of Greek mythology, including references to supernatural events, are accurate depictions of history."
// GroupDescription :
"P2729623461" "Oxford Professor"
// DisplayNames :
"P2580656805" "Dr. James Harvan"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_Antonio_Nash_SSA2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P255036164" "Since the destruction of Galaxy City, the FBSA has been scrambling to reassign its personnel to more effective positions in Paragon City. Antonio Nash, formerly the New Hero Liaison for GIFT, has been reassigned to a more direct investigative role. His focused research on the effects of Superadine flew to the top of the priority list when a group of Trolls, led by Atta, went on a rampage through Skyway City and defeated two prominent members of the Freedom Phalanx. Now Nash has been caught up in the investigation of Pandora's Box, and what possible ties it could have - if any - with the Trolls and their designer drug of choice."
// GroupDescription :
"P500803771" "G.I.F.T. Special Investigator"
// DisplayNames :
"P943755051" "Antonio Nash"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - NPC_Civilians_James_Harvan_SSA2_3_Cutscene 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
