// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Polar_Shift 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1283264660" "Polar Shift was orphaned when a tragic avalanche buried her parent's cabin. She barely survived by becoming one with the bone chilling ice, changing her life forever."
// DisplayNames :
"P1265682120" "Polar Shift"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_No_Mind 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4284762035" "No Mind has devoted his entire life to the study of martial arts and the zen philosophy. Now that his skills are honed to perfection, he can act without thought and fight for balance in the universe."
// DisplayNames :
"P786616566" "No Mind"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_No_Mind_OGT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Rosethorn 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2179084865" "Rosethorn was a brilliant botanist who was kidnapped by a villain working with the Devouring Earth. They were trying to develop human-plant hybrids, and ended up using her as a test subject! After she developed her powers she managed to escape and become the hero known as Rosethorn!"
// DisplayNames :
"P815258051" "Rosethorn"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Arc_Flash 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P791396765" "Thanks to her magical bracers Arc Flash is able to harness the chaotic energies of lightning to blast her foes."
// DisplayNames :
"P3561636179" "Arc Flash"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Arc_Flash_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Doc_Quantum 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2136411672" "Doctor Quantum has used his scientific genius to develop a means of wielding quantum energies to defeat super-powered menaces."
// DisplayNames :
"P574073645" "Doc Quantum"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Ms_Shock 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4056121489" "Ms. Shock is a mutant with the ability to store and discharge electrical energy. She uses her powers to counter super-powered threats."
// DisplayNames :
"P624903972" "Ms. Shock"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Ms_Shock_NoXP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Stalwart 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P279077295" "Stalwart started off as a champion prize fighter. It took him only a short while to discover that his power and abilities never stopped growing by leaps and bounds. After a very brief but undefeated career Stalwart decided he was destined for greater things. Now he fights the evil of the world one left hook at a time."
// DisplayNames :
"P3428454052" "Stalwart"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Stalwart_NoXP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Sky_Dragon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3469032303" "Sky Dragon is master of a mystical martial art known only to a few Eastern sorcerers. He has come to Paragon city to defeat villainy in all its forms."
// DisplayNames :
"P2190177346" "Sky Dragon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Sky_Dragon_NoXP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Overdrive 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3925975470" "Overdrive is a high-energy physics engineer who developed a combat suit to battle villains who threaten the safety of the free world."
// DisplayNames :
"P3158740341" "Overdrive"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Overdrive_NoXP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Blast_Furnace 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P629700019" "Blast Furnace is a mutant who can cause his body to burst into flame. Somewhat uncontrollable, he has taken to wearing armor to contain his awesome energies."
// DisplayNames :
"P958539533" "Blast Furnace"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Cacophony 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2815370731" "Cacophony was a singer whose mutants powers manifested during an opera performance, causing untold mayhem and destruction. Since then she has managed to harness her powers for good."
// DisplayNames :
"P3368508465" "Cacophony"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Holo_Man 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Ravenstorm_Pet 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2462767566" "Joachim Matthias Reinhardt, an exchange student from Berlin, was obsessed with the dark matter that some Magic Origin heroes were able to channel into magnificent powers. Unwilling to tread down a mystical road himself, Joachim was determined to find a way to summon this dark matter through technology. Eventually, he created his "Nano-Noir" technology, which allowed small nannites within his body to store the dark matter and release it on demand. Of all Paragon City's heroes, Ravenstorm is the most solitary. Many find it surprising that he has formed such a close friendship with Moonfire, the Kheldian hero stationed on Striga Isle. But perhaps he considers her, like himself, alone in the world."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2132985917" "Scrapper"
// GroupDescription :
// DisplayNames :
"P2744261059" "Ravenstorm"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Ravenstorm_AV 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_War_Witch_Pet 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2564916453" "Though War Witch has passed away, her spirit remains rooted to the world for which she gave her life. The ghost of War Witch has made her home in Croatoa over the last several months, sitting silently by the lake--but now she has sprung into action. It seems that War Witch's ghost retains the powers granted to her by her mystical coven, and will continue to use them in service of Paragon City."
// DisplayClassName :
"P426732286" "Blaster"
// GroupDescription :
"P2227860250" "LegacyChain"
// DisplayNames :
"P41739984" "War Witch"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_War_Witch_AV 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Icedrone 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2979162974" "Icedrone was a brilliant mechanic who had a project on the side - the creation of super-powered gloves that could control ice.<br><br>He was forced to use a prototype version of his gloves when the Hellions attacked his shop one day. The shop burned to the ground, but Icedrone was able to defeat the Hellions. Icedrone abandoned his career as a mechanic that day to take up fighting crime in Paragon, though he has been known to let his own political views get in the way of his crime-fighting.""
// DisplayNames :
"P2570987591" "Icedrone"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - ParagonHeroes_Victoria_Manuel 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1421587428" "Victoria Manuel was always told she had a sparkle in her eyes for greatness. This sparkle became a reality after a mutation kicked in on her 20th birthday. This glow allows her to predict the movement of her enemies, allowing her to easily dodge their attacks.<br><br>Victoria used her heightened reflexes to train in the art of dual blades, and for a time fought crime in Paragon City. However, she has now retired and become a manager of one of the local theaters in the Promenade.""

